GRAPH <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Digest_Narrative_AntiSlackPositioning> {
  <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Digest_Narrative_AntiSlackPositioning> a narr:Digest ;
    narr:digestOf <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Narrative_AntiSlackPositioning> ;
    narr:childCount "8"^^xsd:integer ;
    narr:generatedFrom "583c388fa21a11eb90e4f3f105450c41067b11da" ;
    narr:narration """This hub gathers the product's anti-Slack positioning, originating from a March 2026 vision session that named [real-time chat as the anti-pattern](narr:Position_AntiPatternRealtimeChat) and defined the product as a [structured async decision platform](narr:Position_ProductCategoryAsyncPlatform) — a deliberate category-creation move against Slack and Teams. The initial go-to-market frame set a [target of remote teams with 10–50 people](narr:Position_TargetMarketRemoteTeams) and [pricing at $12/user/month](narr:Position_PricingTwelveDollars). By July 2026, Sprint 4 delivery evidence is recruited to substantiate the thesis: [Tanya reports shipping the async decision widget](narr:Expr_1E2ETanyaCollab1784543275763_1), [velocity at 23 points — highest that quarter](narr:Expr_1E2ETanyaCollab1784543275763_2), and [the Zephyr integration as the key unlock](narr:Expr_1E2ETanyaCollab1784543275763_3). A [Sprint 4 delivery-proof frame](narr:Position_Sprint4DeliveryProof) explicitly asks what the sprint demonstrates about the anti-Slack thesis, leaving the connection as an open question rather than a settled claim. The pricing note carries an internal update to $15/user for teams over 25, recorded at the Sprint 4 retro, that the positioning children do not yet reflect.""" ;
    narr:covers <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_1E2ETanyaCollab1784543275763_1> ;
    narr:covers <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_1E2ETanyaCollab1784543275763_2> ;
    narr:covers <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_1E2ETanyaCollab1784543275763_3> ;
    narr:covers <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Position_AntiPatternRealtimeChat> ;
    narr:covers <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Position_PricingTwelveDollars> ;
    narr:covers <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Position_ProductCategoryAsyncPlatform> ;
    narr:covers <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Position_Sprint4DeliveryProof> ;
    narr:covers <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Position_TargetMarketRemoteTeams> ;
    narr:keyPhrase [ narr:text "We shipped the async decision widget." ; narr:phraseSource <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_1E2ETanyaCollab1784543275763_1> ] ;
    narr:keyPhrase [ narr:text "Velocity was 23 points, highest this quarter." ; narr:phraseSource <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_1E2ETanyaCollab1784543275763_2> ] ;
    narr:keyPhrase [ narr:text "The Zephyr integration was the key unlock." ; narr:phraseSource <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_1E2ETanyaCollab1784543275763_3> ] ;
    narr:keyPhrase [ narr:text "Real-time chat (Slack, Teams) is the named anti-pattern." ; narr:phraseSource <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Position_AntiPatternRealtimeChat> ] ;
    narr:keyPhrase [ narr:text "Pricing set at $12/user/month as of 2026-03-10 product vision session." ; narr:phraseSource <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Position_PricingTwelveDollars> ] ;
    narr:keyPhrase [ narr:text "Target market: remote teams with 10-50 people." ; narr:phraseSource <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Position_TargetMarketRemoteTeams> ] ;
    narr:variation [ narr:text "Pricing drift: $12/user/month set at the March vision session, but the Sprint 4 retro records $15/user for teams over 25 — the positioning children don't reflect the update." ; narr:over <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Position_PricingTwelveDollars> ] ;
    narr:variation [ narr:text "The Sprint 4 delivery-proof frame is an open question, not a settled claim — whether shipping a widget and hitting velocity actually substantiates the anti-Slack category thesis is left unresolved." ; narr:over <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Position_Sprint4DeliveryProof> ; narr:over <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_1E2ETanyaCollab1784543275763_1> ; narr:over <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_1E2ETanyaCollab1784543275763_2> ] ;
    narr:variation [ narr:text "Delivery evidence is operational and technical (widget shipped, Zephyr integration unlocked velocity) while the positioning thesis is a category-creation claim — the gap between what was demonstrated and what was claimed is not closed." ; narr:over <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_1E2ETanyaCollab1784543275763_3> ; narr:over <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Position_ProductCategoryAsyncPlatform> ] ;
    narr:writer "z-ai/glm-5.2" .
